# Derived state — rebuilt from the ground, never a record.
index/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Scratch the seats write. The record is SEAT_LOG.md and memory.md, not this.
agent_workspace/

# Proposals not yet landed by the operator.
memory/pending.jsonl

# Run transcripts. Every run writes one, so versioning them left the ground
# permanently dirty -- session 6's second commit was nothing but the logs of
# its first. The durable record is SEAT_LOG.md and memory.md; logs/ is the
# working trace behind them and stays on disk, just untracked.
logs/

# Binaries and weights: whisper.cpp lives here so the CLI is self-contained,
# but 144MB of .exe/.dll/.bin is not source and does not go in the record.
bin/

# Keys are silent (LAW 9).
.env

# The operator's archive of his own work. Local only, left alone, never
# versioned here. Operator's ruling 2026-09-02.
#
# ADDING THIS DID NOT UNTRACK WHAT WAS ALREADY TRACKED: 383 files under
# worlds/ (268 of them under a vault/) entered history at e1c0ae6 and 0bfd8c4.
# `git rm -r --cached worlds/` was run by the operator (d0d6426, 2026-09-02);
# `git ls-files worlds/` is 0. The two old commits still hold them. The existing commits are a separate question and
# LAW 1 cuts against rewriting them.
#
# THAT REASONING EXPIRED 2026-09-10. This line used to end "Not an exposure
# while this repo has no remote -- it has never had one." The repo now has a
# remote and it has been public. The CONCLUSION still holds, and it was
# checked rather than assumed: `git rev-list --objects origin/main` finds ZERO
# paths under worlds/, because those three commits (d0d6426, 0bfd8c4, e1c0ae6)
# are local history that was never pushed. But it holds by fact, not by the
# argument that used to sit here, and a safety note resting on a premise that
# has changed is worse than no note.
#
# THE SAME COMMITS MAKE `git bundle --all` CARRY THE VAULT -- 240 MB against
# 2.3 MB for `git bundle create <file> main`. Bundle the BRANCH, never --all,
# when the bundle leaves this machine.
worlds/

# Packaging artifacts. `pip install .` / `python -m build` leave these in the
# ground; they are generated, never authored. Added 2026-09-03 with
# pyproject.toml -- the first commit after it would otherwise have tracked a
# build tree.
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# The ledger, the seat log and the memory are written by the chain at every
# open, toll, land and close, so a tracked copy made the ground DIRTY before
# the operator typed a word (TASKS, the REPL read of 2026-09-08). Operator's
# ruling 2026-09-08: "dont git track them." They stay on disk as the record;
# git holds the code and the docs. Adding these lines does not untrack what
# is already tracked -- `git rm --cached` of each is the operator's act
# (RULE 6), as it was for worlds/ on 2026-09-02.
sessions/*.jsonl
SEAT_LOG.md
memory.md

# Build leavings. whisper.cpp's binaries live under bin/ above; these catch
# anything a compiler drops in the ground itself.
*.exe
*.exe~
*.obj
node_modules/
.venv/

# ATLAS IS ITS OWN REPOSITORY (2026-09-10, the operator's word: "let's get the
# core and atlas split"). It was 509 of this repo's 682 tracked files -- three
# quarters of the ground -- versioned on its own VERSION (0.1.1+f1) against the
# core's 0.1.9, with its own CHANGELOG, HANDOFF, SEAT_LOG, roster, go.mod and
# Cargo.toml. Two projects sharing one history, and only one of them was ever
# proven by this repo's CI.
#
# It STAYS AT atlas/ -- RULE 1, the ground is Research and nothing leaves it --
# but it carries its own .git, its own history (extracted whole with
# `git subtree split`, 20 commits, nothing rewritten) and its own ignores.
# The seam between them is a runtime path, not a build dependency: atlas reads
# the ground through `t.Home`, and manjuel/ imports nothing from atlas.
#
# The files were untracked here with `git rm -r --cached atlas`; the history
# that holds them is untouched, as LAW 1 requires.
atlas/
